  "steps": [
    "Heat the oil in a large stockpot over medium-low heat.",
    "Add the onion and cook on low until lightly translucent, 3-4 min. Add the celery, carrot, cauliflower rice, and garlic and cook until slightly softened, about 5 min.",
    "Pour in the broth and lemon juice, and add the dill, most of the parsley, the salt, and the pepper. Stir, raise the heat to medium, and simmer 15 min.",
    "Add the cooked chicken and kale and stir until the kale wilts and the chicken is hot, 4-5 min.",
    "(Skip for AIP.) Whisk the egg yolks in a small bowl. Ladle out about 1 cup of the hot broth and pour it into the yolks in a slow stream while whisking constantly. Stir the yolk mixture back into the pot and remove from the heat; do not let it boil again or the yolks will curdle.",
    "Let the soup cool a few minutes, taste for salt, and serve with lemon wedges, a little zest, and the reserved parsley."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Leftover or rotisserie chicken works here; the soup only warms it through."
  ],
